// OJZ replay fixture — the standing regression-net input stream (spec
// 2026-08-02 §4). Recorded by the overseer harness session (I4); packed by
// tools/replay_pack.py. Placed after ALL GAMEPLAY content but BEFORE the
// fault-handler island (ReleaseFault / the error_handler MDDBG blob), which the
// deb2 symbol-table contract requires to be the final byte-emitting section —
// the blob's two baked `lea` displacements point at blob end, so nothing may be
// appended after it (see engine/debug/error_handler.emp's WARNING and the
// INVARIANT block in games/sonic4/map.toml). So re-recording (a content+size
// change) still shifts ZERO gameplay addresses — the fixture build and the
// recording build agree on every address the curated hash covers — but it DOES
// shift the fault-handler island and EndOfRom. That island is pure
// fault-handling equipment, carries no gameplay state, and `repin` re-pins it.
// Playback entry: Replay_Ptr = Replay_OJZ_Fixture + REPLAY_HEADER_LEN,
// Input_Source = INPUT_PLAYBACK (oracle poke recipe in the evidence note).
module games.sonic4.replay_fixture in replay_fixture

pub data Replay_OJZ_Fixture (align: 2) = embed("games/sonic4/data/replays/ojz_fixture.bin")

// OJZ SLIDE fixture — the entity-window coverage the standing fixture does not
// have. Recorded 2026-08-07 (1496 ticks, 24 checkpoints, 240 bytes): run right
// across the section-1 boundary collecting its rings, run left back across it,
// then fly down across the section-row boundary and back up — all four crossing
// directions, with the anchor read after each. The shipped
// `Replay_OJZ_Fixture` never leaves section 0 —
// measured, both carts, in the migmask A/B — so `EntityWindow_Slide`,
// `MigrateMasks`, `PopulateSectionRings` and `InitSection`'s compare-clear had
// ZERO automated behavioural coverage. This stream exercises all of them, and
// the leftward crossing is the one direction that seats a populated surviving
// section on a MISREAD entry.
//
// Proven to FAIL on a cart built with the old x22 stride: the engine's own
// duplicate tripwire fires at `EntityWindow_TrySpawnRing` with the key word
// $0100 (section $01, list index $00) at Logic_Tick 391, and the same stream
// completes clean with Replay_Done=$FF on the fixed cart. A regression net that
// passes on the broken build tests nothing; this one does not.
//
// Vertical crossings need no level-data change: this scene arms CHEAT_DEBUG_FLY
// itself under `if DEBUG == 1`, so free flight is reachable from input alone and
// replays deterministically. The act grid is 3x3, not 3x1.
pub data Replay_OJZ_Slide_Fixture (align: 2) = embed("games/sonic4/data/replays/ojz_slide_fixture.bin")
